WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.835
-Our next guess is a great actor
who stars in and produced

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.571
the new movie "Archenemy,"

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:08.140
which is theaters, on demand,
and on digital next Friday.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.309
Here is Joe Manganiello!

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:12.244
Yo! Wow!

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:14.647
-Hey, Jim.
-Lookin' good, bud.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.582
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Is that...

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:19.452
Is that real? No more...
-This is real.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:22.622
This is freshly shaved
as of this morning.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.989
-Wow!
-Yeah.

00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:27.527
-No more Mohawk.
-No more Mohawk.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.828
But it's amazing how much --

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.996
Like, a Mohawk
is that much hair.

00:00:30.996 --> 00:00:33.833
But you take it off,
and you're freezing.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.136 line:0%
-Joe, what am I see
in the corner of the screen?

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:39.138 line:0%
Is there a special guest?
-[ Chuckles ] Yeah.

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:41.608
This is my sidekick.
-Yes!

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.209
-This is -- This is --
-Oh, no!

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.511
This is -- This is Bubbles.

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:47.547
-Bubbles. Hi, Bubbles.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.715
Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:51.951
I appreciate it. Oh, my gosh.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:55.087
-How cute is that. Oh, my God.
-This is Bubbles'

00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:56.956
first appearance
on "The Tonight Show."

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.125
-And will not be her last.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.660
So, Bubbles, you're allowed back
whenever.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.061
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:04.063
-Joe, there's a ton of stuff
I want to talk to you about,

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:06.432
But, first, congrats.
I know you just celebrated

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:08.234
your five-year
wedding anniversary

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.937
with your lovely wife,
Sofía Vergara.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.605
Congrats on that.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:16.108
We've talked before about how
you and Sofía started dating.

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:19.745
But you -- were you always
smooth when it came to dating?

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:22.114
Because I want to know
about this guy.

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:26.586
This...
-That guy -- not so smooth

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.456
with the dating, Jimmy.
Yeah, not so smooth.

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:32.491
-Look at the arms, bud.
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:36.128
-Mm-hmm.
-Dude, when did it change?

00:01:36.128 --> 00:01:38.097
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:42.502
-It changed around age 16.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:45.905
Then, I got contact lenses,

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:49.808
and the working out
was starting to happen.

00:01:49.808 --> 00:01:53.045
All the protein shakes
were starting to take effect.

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:59.652
And I also -- I got a phone call
from a friend of mine,

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:02.755
who said, you know, "How'd you
like to make 25 bucks an hour?"

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.224
At age 16, you say, "Sure.
What do I have to do?"

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:07.793
They said, "Just come down
to our office.

00:02:07.793 --> 00:02:09.628
Whatever anybody says to you,

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:12.165
what they ask,
just say you're 21."

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:14.200
And I didn't have a license
at this time,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.036
so I had to have my mother come
drop me off at their office.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.871
And there was a bunch of adults,
and they said --

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.739
you know, I walked in, they
said, "You're the guy?"

00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:22.308
I said, "Yeah."
They said, "How old are you?"

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.610
I said, "21."
They go, "Great. Put this on."

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.812
And they handed me
this pirate suit,

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:30.183
with the cape and the eye patch
and the wig and the ruffles,

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.685
the hat, I had a sword.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.188
I had a pistola.

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:37.857
The little fake booties
that go over your shoes

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.826
to make them look
like they're real boots.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:42.661
-Yeah. What were you?
-And I was gonna go

00:02:42.661 --> 00:02:46.065
be Captain Morgan at a bunch
of bars in Pittsburgh.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.433
-Wow!

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.701
-And they gave me a backpack
that was a tank

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:52.505
with a tap on it, full of rum.
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.373
-So I went --
-Do you still have that?

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:58.411
-Go get everyone drunk.
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:02.047
-So, that led to, like,

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:04.583
you know, probably
the next decade,

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:06.786
I worked in bars.
You know, that's how I worked

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:08.388
until, like, acting took off

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:11.157
where I could pay my bills
that way as an artist.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:14.060
I was working in clubs,
and so, like,

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.563
that Captain Morgan job,
then, when I was 21 --

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:19.999
I worked as Captain Morgan
in Pittsburgh from 16 to 21.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.233
And then, when I was 21,

00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:23.335
I got a job working
for Finlandia vodka,

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:28.707
where I would go out U2's
old tour bus full of vodka.

00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:30.810
We would drive to every
major city in America.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.012
I was in a tuxedo this time.
It was a little classier.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.947
-Yeah, you upped your game.
-Get everybody drunk.

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:38.451
So it was, like, just nonstop
wall-to-wall bar jump.

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:41.287
But what the point is,
circling back, is

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:46.859
that that was the best education
in men and women and dating.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.862
When you are in a club,
night after night,

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.732
watching the animals hunt
in the wild...

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.667
-Wow.
-...you learn a lot.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:59.405
So that scrawny kid really got
his formal education

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:03.342
in women and men and dating
and all that.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:05.178
-And look at you now.
I mean, come on.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:07.947
I mean, we know you
as this giant movie star.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:11.984
And I know that, growing up,
wasn't your original dream

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:15.687
to also be
a writer and director?

00:04:15.687 --> 00:04:17.790
-Well, yeah, as a kid,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.491
that's actually
how I got into acting.

00:04:19.491 --> 00:04:21.160
I made all my own movies,

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:25.765
where you do, like,
Mafia martial arts movies...

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:28.601
with, like, gunshots
and, you know, squib.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.070
We made homemade squibs
when we were kids.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:34.673
-You made a homemade squib,
like a blood-explosion squib?

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:38.177
-Yeah, so, we would take
a firecracker,

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:41.047
and then you'd take a condom
and you'd fill the condom

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.216
with Karo syrup
and red food coloring.

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:46.285
You tie it up.
And you get a cookie tin.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:49.722
And you could, like --
If you got really brave,

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:51.891
you'd put the cookie tin,
like, over your heart.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.093
So we'd cut the shirt
a little bit,

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.794
so the wick would come out.

00:04:55.794 --> 00:04:58.264
And then you had to turn
the camera on someone's hand.

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:02.534
They had to come in
and light the lighter, the wick,

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:04.971
and then get your hand out
so that we could get the shot.

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:07.340
"Oh!" You know, and
you'd fall over

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.275
and, you know, have
this flap of skin,

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:11.109
and blood would gush out
everywhere.

00:05:11.109 --> 00:05:14.414
-Joe, that was probably
a real flap of real skin.

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:17.783
You lit a firecracker
on someone's chest.

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:19.552
-It was --
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:23.322
-Yeah, it was painful, yeah.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:27.493
That is unbelievable.
Uh, uh, I, uh --

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.361
I want to talk
about your new movie.

00:05:29.361 --> 00:05:32.464
It's called "Archenemy."
And I love the premise.

00:05:32.464 --> 00:05:34.766
I've never seen
a movie like this.

00:05:34.766 --> 00:05:37.804
I would say it's
a superhero movie.

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:39.839
But it's more than
a superhero movie.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:42.875 line:0%
It's -- It's a trickier plot.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:45.110 line:0%
Basically -- DO you want me
to set it up?

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:47.579 line:0%
You basically land
on a planet.

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:50.483 line:0%
And you're like,
"On Earth, I'm a superhero."

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:53.720 line:0%
-Well, maybe. You don't know.
-Right.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:56.989 line:0%
-That's the thing, is, like,
everything that you just said

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.658 line:0%
is absolutely true, you know,
but, you know,

00:05:59.658 --> 00:06:01.860 line:0%
is it a superhero movie,
or is it not?

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:04.463 line:0%
Because, really,
the bulk of it is,

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:10.169 line:0%
I play a maybe borderline
schizophrenic character

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:15.007 line:0%
who's also addicted to
methamphetamine and alcohol

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.943 line:0%
and lives in a tent
under a bridge

00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:18.644 line:0%
and babbles on and on and on

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.612 line:0%
to anybody
who will listen to him

00:06:20.612 --> 00:06:23.882 line:0%
about being
some sort of champion

00:06:23.882 --> 00:06:27.586 line:0%
or Superman, superhero
from another dimension.

00:06:27.586 --> 00:06:32.458 line:0%
So, really, is an exploration
about whether or not

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:35.761 line:0%
he's crazy,
or is it actually true.

00:06:35.761 --> 00:06:39.499
-Again, I don't like to spoil
anything, but it's great.

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:40.633
And I want to
show everyone a clip.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:42.902
Here's Joe Manganiello
in "Archenemy."

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.270
Take a look.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.804
-You cannot run.

00:06:45.804 --> 00:06:48.307
Hey, I don't care what you do.

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:50.242
You make bad choices,
you live with them.

00:06:50.242 --> 00:06:52.478
It's fine, but the kid deserves
his own chance.

00:06:54.379 --> 00:06:57.483
If you run, they will find you,
and they will kill him.

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:02.488
-So, what are we supposed to do?

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:04.290
-You stay and you fight the war.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.692
-Hamster, don't engage
with the troll.

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:08.895
-Fight the war?
-[ Scoffs ]

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:10.762
-How are we supposed to do that?

00:07:10.762 --> 00:07:13.399
-Don't undersell yourself.

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:15.167
I'm here with you.

00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:17.269
I fell through a black hole
to get here.

00:07:17.269 --> 00:07:20.106
And I never knew why until now.

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:23.509
It was so I could help you.

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:25.611
Both of you.

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:31.617
♪♪

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:33.919 line:0%
-Aww. What did you think, buddy?
Oh, he loved it.

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:35.454 line:0%
[ Chuckling ] He loved it.

00:07:35.454 --> 00:07:37.556 line:0%
Joe Manganiello, everybody.

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:40.726 line:0%
"Archenemy" is in theaters,
on demand, and on digital,

00:07:40.726 --> 00:07:42.294 line:0%
starting December 11th.

00:07:42.294 --> 00:07:43.896 line:0%
Thank you so much
for coming on, bud.

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:47.266 line:0%
It's always great to see you.
-Hey, man, thank you so much.

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:48.667 line:0%
I love being here.
It's so great.

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:50.069 line:0%
I have so much fun with you.
-Stay safe.

